{
  "id": "s02-l05",
  "unit": "s02-consonants",
  "title": "Consonants 5: প ফ ব ভ ম",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Row 5 is made with the lips: **প ফ ব ভ ম**. After four rows you know the pattern: plain, puffed, voiced, voiced-puffed, nasal.\n\n**ফ** is officially a puffed p, but in Bangladesh it's usually a plain **f**: ফল (`fol`, *fruit*). **ভ** is a breathy b that can sound like *v*: ভালো (`bhalo`, *good*).\n\n**ব** is the shape to memorise carefully: a simple triangle hanging from the top line. In the next lesson you'll meet **র**, which is ব plus a dot underneath. Many words depend on that dot!\n\n**ম** (`mo`) is the m in মানুষ (`manush`, *person*) and in family words you'll read soon (মা, মামা).",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-pa",
      "bn": "প",
      "tr": "po",
      "en": "p as in 'spin' (no puff)",
      "notes": "Name: po (প)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-pha",
      "bn": "ফ",
      "tr": "fo",
      "en": "f, or a puffed p (between 'ph' and 'f')",
      "notes": "Name: fo/pho (ফ). Most Bangladeshis say a clear f (ফল fol)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ba",
      "bn": "ব",
      "tr": "bo",
      "en": "b as in 'bat'",
      "notes": "Name: bo (ব), also borgio bo (বর্গীয় ব). Shape: a plain triangle hanging from the line. র is ব with a dot below."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-bha",
      "bn": "ভ",
      "tr": "bho",
      "en": "bh: breathy b, often close to 'v'",
      "notes": "Name: bho (ভ). First letter of ভালো."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ma",
      "bn": "ম",
      "tr": "mo",
      "en": "m as in 'mother'",
      "notes": "Name: mo (ম)."
    }
  ],
